// Drift-oracle fixture: `main` declares a static fuel bound (100) that PASSES
// static verification (loopless body). The runtime VM's profile-vs-declared
// drift warning is advisory and NON-gating: a run that stays within the bound
// must succeed without any warning, and the warning (when the runtime fuel
// exceeds the declared bound) never changes exit semantics.
//
// Note: after the soundness fixes for issue #262 (review round 2), a
// fuel-annotated `main` containing a loop cannot pass static verification
// (loop `decreases` is unsatisfiable under immutability, and a shadowed
// variant is rejected fail-closed). The drift warning therefore fires only on
// the out-of-fuel path where the runtime consumed more than the declared
// bound; this fixture exercises the within-bound (no-warning) and the
// non-gating properties.
fn main() -> Int
  [ fuel 100; ]
{
  let a: Int = 1;
  let b: Int = 2;
  return a + b;
}
